/-!
# A hyperplane in projective space is projective space of one lower dimension

A *hyperplane* in `ℙⁿ_k = Proj k[T₀, …, Tₙ]` is the zero scheme `H = Z(s)` of a nonzero global
section `s` of `𝒪(1)`, and such a section is a nonzero homogeneous form `l` of degree one. This
file produces an isomorphism `ℙ^{n-1}_k ≅ H` under which `𝒪(1)` pulls back to `𝒪(1)`.

The route is the source's. A graded surjection `ψ : 𝒮 → ℬ` whose kernel is the ideal generated by
a degree-one element `l` has `Proj ψ` a closed immersion, and over the standard open `D₊(f)` of a
degree-one element the kernel of `Proj ψ` on sections is generated by the single fraction `l / f`,
which is also the local equation of `Z(s)`. So the two closed subschemes have the same ideal sheaf
and are canonically isomorphic, and the twists match by [Stacks, Tag 01N1] part (3). For the
polynomial ring such a `ψ` comes from the quotient `k^{n+1} → k^{n+1} / ⟨l⟩` by reading `l` as a
vector through a basis: the kernel of `Sym` of a surjection is generated by the kernel of the
surjection, and the symmetric algebra of a space with a basis indexed by `Fin n` is a polynomial
ring in `n` variables.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.hyperplane`: the hyperplane of a degree-one form, the zero scheme of the
  global section of `𝒪(1)` it determines.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.hyperplaneOfSection`: the hyperplane of an arbitrary global section of
  `𝒪(1)`, the source's own presentation.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.exists_mem_mul_eq_of_mem_span_degreeOne`: a homogeneous multiple of a
  degree-one element has a homogeneous cofactor.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.ker_app_projMap_basicOpen`: the kernel of `Proj ψ` on a standard chart
  is generated by the chart fraction `l / f`.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.ker_projMap_eq_zeroScheme`: the ideal sheaf of `Proj ℬ` in `Proj 𝒮` is
  the zero scheme of the degree-one section `l`.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.nonempty_pullbackTwist_projMap`: the twists pull back along `Proj ψ`.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.exists_iso_zeroScheme_subscheme_pullbackTwist`: the two previous results
  combined — `Proj ℬ` is the zero scheme of `l`, compatibly with all twists.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.exists_gradedHom_ker_span_degreeOne`: the graded surjection
  `k[T₀, …, Tₙ] → k[S₀, …, S_{n-1}]` with kernel a given nonzero degree-one form.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.exists_iso_projectiveSpace_hyperplane`: **the hyperplane of a nonzero
  degree-one form is `ℙ^{n-1}_k`, and `𝒪(1)` pulls back to `𝒪(1)`.**
* `Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.exists_iso_projectiveSpace_hyperplaneOfSection`: **the same for the
  hyperplane of an arbitrary nonzero global section of `𝒪(1)`**, which is the statement of
  [Stacks, Tag 089Z]. Like the previous result it also reports that the identification is a
  morphism over `Spec k`, which is what the hyperplane restriction data of [Stacks, Tag 08A7]
  consumes.

## Implementation notes

`ℙⁿ_k` is read as `Proj k[T₀, …, Tₙ]`, which is the source's own formula and the model the
twisting sheaf `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.twistingSheaf` of [Stacks, Tag 01MN]
lives on. The base-change model `AlgebraicGeometry.projectiveSpaceOverRing` of [Stacks, Tag 01NF]
is identified with it by `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjBaseChange.isIso_projCompare`, over
`Spec k`; that identification is not performed here and no statement below mentions it.

## From a form to an arbitrary section

The source takes an arbitrary nonzero global section `s` of `𝒪(1)` and only then observes that `s`
"corresponds to a homogeneous form in `T₀, …, Tₙ` of degree 1", citing the computation of
`Γ(ℙⁿ_k, 𝒪(d))` of [Stacks, Tag 01XS]. Everything below the final theorem presents the hyperplane
by the form; that observation is
`Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.Cohomology.exists_degreeSection_eq`, which says that
`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.degreeSection` in degree one is onto all of
`Γ(ℙⁿ_k, 𝒪(1))`, and
`Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.exists_iso_projectiveSpace_hyperplaneOfSection` is the two put together.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 089Z](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/089Z)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 089Y](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/089Y)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N1)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03GL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03GL)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

